From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:27:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] backup, davsync: a full library's backup seals compressed,
 within what GitHub's file API takes (#2707)

GitHub's file API refused the reporter's 54.7 MiB sealed backup as too
large (HTTP 422) while magpie's own guard allows 64 MiB, so a populated
library could not sync to GitHub at all: the sealed file carries the
bundle base64-encoded twice (the bundle's JSON, then the envelope's),
which alone takes 32 MiB of carried skill files to about 57 MiB.

What changed:
- Seal compresses the bundle before encrypting it (envelope version 2).
  A version 2 file tells an older magpie "made by a newer magpie"; a
  version 1 file an older magpie sealed plainly still opens here. The
  skill-files cap's size arithmetic (internal/library/carry.go) follows.
- A write GitHub refuses as too large names the file's size and the
  backends a backup that big fits, instead of the bare 422's words.
- docs/subsystems/sync-backup.md says both.

Run: go test -tags nogui ./internal/backup ./internal/davsync
./internal/library ./internal/cli (ok); gofmt -l clean; go vet and go
build on darwin/arm64, linux/amd64, windows/amd64. Ablation at this
commit's parent (8233eada), every product file of this commit removed,
tests kept: TestSealCompressesTheLibrary red (58,255,516 bytes sealed
from a 43,691,485-byte library, no compression) and
TestGitHubFailures/file_too_large red (generic 422 text); restored,
both green. Not tried against the real GitHub API; the compressed size
is asserted below the 54.7 MiB the API refused in the report.

